{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.hecke_root_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.hecke_root_product","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L247-L249","doc":"Its two roots multiply to `−1`: the `det T = −1` of the arc, on any block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.hecke_quadratic_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.hecke_quadratic_factor","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L241-L245","doc":"The Hecke quadratic `x² − h x − 1` with `h = q − q⁻¹` factors as `(x − q)(x + q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.seminormal_radicand_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.seminormal_radicand_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L232-L239","doc":"In an ordered field the radicand is non-negative whenever `|h/(u − u⁻¹)| ≤ 1`, i.e.\n`|[ρ]_q| ≥ 1` — so the `abs` in `sqrt(|a a' + 1|)` is a no-op there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.seminormal_radicand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.seminormal_radicand","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L227-L230","doc":"Hence the off-diagonal radicand is `1 − (h/(u − u⁻¹))²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.seminormal_diag_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.seminormal_diag_product","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L209-L225","doc":"The two diagonal entries of a branching seminormal block multiply to `−(h/(u − u⁻¹))²`,\ni.e. `−1/[ρ]_q²` once `h = q − q⁻¹` and `u = q^ρ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.cum_eq_zero_of_additive_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.cum_eq_zero_of_additive_split","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L150-L201","doc":"**Mixed cumulants of an additive set function vanish.** If the ground set splits as\n`A ⊔ B` and `L` is additive across the split, every cumulant straddling it is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.filter_powerset_not_subset_subset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.filter_powerset_not_subset_subset","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L134-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.filter_powerset_subset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.filter_powerset_subset","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L129-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.cum_eq_sizeCum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.cum_eq_sizeCum","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L114-L125","doc":"**The size-only collapse.** If `L` depends only on cardinality, so do its cumulants, and\nthey obey the scalar recursion. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:subset-cumulant-recursion","label":"prop:subset-cumulant-recursion","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/subset-cumulant-recursion.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.sum_powerset_erase_apply_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.sum_powerset_erase_apply_card","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L104-L112","doc":"Summing a function of the cardinality over the *proper* subsets of `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.sizeCum_zero_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.sizeCum_zero_one","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L97-L102","doc":"With no zero- or one-body term the recursion starts at `k = 2`, as the probes write it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.sizeCum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.sizeCum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L93-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.sizeCum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.sizeCum","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L87-L91","doc":"The scalar recursion for an exchangeable system: `c_k = f_k − Σ_{j<k} C(k,j) c_j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.sum_powerset_cum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.sum_powerset_cum","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L78-L83","doc":"**Reconstruction.** The cumulants of the subsets of `S` sum back to `L S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.cum_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.cum_empty","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L75-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.cum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.cum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L71-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.cum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubsetCumulantRecursion.cum","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubsetCumulantRecursion.lean#L61-L69","doc":"Möbius cumulants of a set function, by the recursion the probes run:\n`cum L S = L S − Σ_{T ⊊ S} cum L T`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}